rotocol_hash":"54fbd25c87110ea1b813f57c205b1725ceb0fb77b1e61ed9a331e3fe90dc6d31","report_ref":{"availability":"available","sha256":"78d32fcc624b508fe3c1c8793efc68dd22309682afa65e9419c6f04a4f8ce225","size":10888},"scientific_conclusion":"unknown","scientific_unit":"declared development seed aggregate; not additional independent runs or category slices","seed_ids":[42],"source_experiment_ids":["amazon-next-v7-round-5-control-1-CDs_and_Vinyl-42","amazon-next-v7-round-5-control-1-Electronics-42","amazon-next-v7-round-5-control-1-Industrial_and_Scientific-42","amazon-next-v7-round-5-control-1-Movies_and_TV-42","amazon-next-v7-round-5-model-CDs_and_Vinyl-42","amazon-next-v7-round-5-model-Electronics-42","amazon-next-v7-round-5-model-Industrial_and_Scientific-42","amazon-next-v7-round-5-model-Movies_and_TV-42","selected_v3-CDs_and_Vinyl-42","selected_v3-Electronics-42","selected_v3-Industrial_and_Scientific-42","selected_v3-Movies_and_TV-42"],"status":"success","task_id":"amazon-research-9b51668f86f6f404","valid":true,"visibility":"public"},"id":"amazon-research-9b51668f86f6f404-f83a2bcad14a55d9-development","type":"Experiment"},{"attrs":{"affected_components":["model.py: NextItNetBlock.__init__","model.py: NextItNetBlock.forward"],"alternative_explanations":["The existing unconditional residual addition may be optimal under this protocol.","Any ranking change could arise from optimization, added parameters, or checkpoint selection rather than useful conditioning."],"cheapest_discriminating_test":"Without training, use identical fixed block inputs and convolution outputs in both arms. Verify that zero gate parameters reproduce the incumbent block exactly, then set nonzero parameters and vary the input while holding the convolution output fixed. The candidate gate should respond to the input; the matched control gate should not. This tests the implementation, not ranking benefit.","gap_id":"amazon-next-v7-round-5-residual-conditioning","model_version":"selected_v3","observation_refs":["current-baseline-0b9b74a7cf77fd8200690b25"],"origin":"agent_hypothesis","predicted_observations":["At initialization, both gated arms reproduce the incumbent residual output.","After nonzero gate updates, the two arms differ on fixed-state inputs designed to separate input conditioning from update conditioning.","If input-conditioned residual scaling helps ranking, the candidate exceeds both the incumbent and matched control under the frozen evaluation."],"protocol_hash":"54fbd25c87110ea1b813f57c205b1725ceb0fb77b1e61ed9a331e3fe90dc6d31","status":"unknown","suspected_capability":"Conditioning each causal convolutional update on its incoming state may improve ranking. The inspected block adds its update unconditionally; the supplied graph does not establish that this causes a deficit.","task_context":"Observed graph fact: selected_v3 seed-42 HR@10 is 0.619, 0.546, 0.445 and 0.643 across Movies_and_TV, Industrial_and_Scientific, Electronics and CDs_and_Vinyl, for an unweighted mean of 0.56325. The supplied graph has no counterevidence, alternative or revision edges; absence of those edges is not support for the proposed mechanism. The ranking explanation and predicted benefit are provisional. Historical development selection outcomes do not establish or refute this mechanism.","task_id":"amazon-research-9b51668f86f6f404","visibility":"public"},"id":"amazon-research-9b51668f86f6f404-f83a2bcad14a55d9-gap","type":"GapHypothesis"},{"attrs":{"baseline":"selected_v3","candidate":"amazon-next-v7-round-5-model","candidate_minus_baseline":0.0024999999999999467,"candidate_minus_control":0.0022499999999999742,"control":"amazon-next-v7-round-5-control-1","control_minus_baseline":0.00024999999999997247,"design":{"alternative_explanations":["Extra parameters or changed gradient flow, rather than input conditioning, may explain a gain.","Input and update gates can have different activation distributions despite matched capacity.","Stochastic training and public-validation checkpoint selection may explain small differences."],"falsification_condition":"Reject implementation admission if initialization equivalence, the conditioning diagnostic, causality or scoring contracts fail. Do not advance if seed-42 candidate-minus-incumbent mean HR@10 is <=0.005, candidate-minus-control is <=0, or the frozen eligibility gate fails. If eligible, apply only the existing confirmation rules to independent seeds 202609291 and 202609292. A control advantage or failure to reproduce the effect weakens the input-conditioning explanation.","insertion_contract":"{\"schema\":\"nextitnet-method-scope-v1\",\"allowed_methods\":[\"NextItNetBlock.__init__\",\"NextItNetBlock.forward\"],\"rationale\":\"Add matched zero-initialized per-channel gate parameters in each block. Candidate scales the existing causal update using the incoming state; the complete generated control scales it using the update. Preserve every other method and the frozen protocol.\"}","mechanism":"Compare one input-conditioned residual gate against selected_v3 and a parameter-matched update-conditioned gate. The matched gate control separates the proposed conditioning choice from the shared addition of gate parameters, subject to remaining optimization differences.","predicted_observations":["At initialization, both gated arms reproduce the incumbent residual output.","After nonzero gate updates, the two arms differ on fixed-state inputs designed to separate input conditioning from update conditioning.","If input-conditioned residual scaling helps ranking, the candidate exceeds both the incumbent and matched control under the frozen evaluation."]},"design_hash":"b3d8d45efe31dc34d42e105464858799446dff6732e07cd71a4c1f4330c1584a","evidence_dependency_ids":["amazon-research-9b51668f86f6f404-f83a2bcad14a55d9-development"],"independent_unit":false,"kind":"mechanism_comparison","mechanism_status":"unknown","next_step":"Assess whether the implemented contrast isolates the proposed mechanism; design a discriminating follow-up for competing explanations.","origin":"local_evidence","partition":"development","protocol_hash":"54fbd25c87110ea1b813f57c205b1725ceb0fb77b1e61ed9a331e3fe90dc6d31","qualification":"Paired development observation, not causal proof or independent replication.","report_ref":{"availability":"available","sha256":"78d32fcc624b508fe3c1c8793efc68dd22309682afa65e9419c6f04a4f8ce225","size":10888},"slices":[{"candidate_minus_control":0.020000000000000018,"dataset":"Movies_and_TV","seed":42},{"candidate_minus_control":-0.006000000000000005,"dataset":"Industrial_and_Scientific","seed":42},{"candidate_minus_control":-0.0050000000000000044,"dataset":"Electronics","seed":42},{"candidate_minus_control":0.0,"dataset":"CDs_and_Vinyl","seed":42}],"source_hashes":{"amazon-next-v7-round-5-control-1":"c0fb4d929d6e4bb1af5b9dc2366cdab8c7abe6f44a473257e312510d2e6ea019","amazon-next-v7-round-5-model":"c6ee9202203962ffd5237bf69042a89726f7f7a354621718af9df67281f9a30d","selected_v3":"ae556df7a0c0808bd7c2dc5dc912eb5546a0abe297cc73683a395bddb8240635"},"task_id":"amazon-research-9b51668f86f6f404","visibility":"public"},"id":"amazon-research-9b51668f86f6f404-f83a2bcad14a55d9-mechanism-c00d690da2c980bc","type":"Observation"},{"attrs":{"cost":"Two trainable hidden-width vectors per block; linear elementwise work per block position. Runtime and ranking effects are unmeasured.","insertion_points":["model.py: NextItNetBlock.__init__","model.py: NextItNetBlock.forward","control-1.py: the same two methods"],"mechanism":"Agent hypothesis. For block input x and existing convolutional update y, replace x+y with x+2*sigmoid(w*x+b)*y, using broadcast per-channel trainable vectors w and b initialized to zero. The generated control uses x+2*sigmoid(w*y+b)*y with identical parameter shapes and initialization. Both gates initially equal one; the contrast tests whether conditioning on the incoming state helps beyond conditioning on the update.","method_id":"amazon-next-v7-input-conditioned-residual","origin":"agent_hypothesis","prerequisites":["Admit complete candidate and control modules with changes confined to the declared methods.","Run CPU contracts before any fit.","Initialize each category, seed and arm independently under the frozen protocol."],"protocol_hash":"54fbd25c87110ea1b813f57c205b1725ceb0fb77b1e61ed9a331e3fe90dc6d31","sources":[],"task_id":"amazon-research-9b51668f86f6f404","tensor_constraints":["Keep each block input and output shape [batch,length,hidden], dtype and device.","Gate only the existing causal update; introduce no future-position reads.","Preserve encode_sequence output shape [batch,length,hidden], padding mask and finite empty-history behavior.","Preserve forward use of encode_sequence and score_candidates = item_emb(candidates) @ encode_sequence(seq)[0,-1], including after learning."],"visibility":"public"},"id":"amazon-research-9b51668f86f6f404-f83a2bcad14a55d9-method","type":"Method"},{"attrs":{"action":"replace","alternative_explanations":["Extra parameters or changed gradient flow, rather than input conditioning, may explain a gain.","Input and update gates can have different activation distributions despite matched capacity.","Stochastic training and public-validation checkpoint selection may explain small differences."],"base_model_id":"selected_v3","budget":1000000,"controls":["selected_v3","amazon-next-v7-round-5-control-1"],"correctness_checks":["With zero gate parameters and dropout disabled, both new arms match the incumbent block output within float32 tolerance.","With copied common weights and nonzero gate parameters, verify the fixed-state conditioning contrast and finite outputs.","Before and after synthetic parameter updates, verify prefix causality, zero padding-embedding gradient, finite empty histories, input immutability, batch independence and permutation equivariance.","Before and after updates, verify forward scoring identities, tail candidate scoring and save/load equivalence.","Verify candidate and generated control have matching parameter counts, state-dict structure and independent initialization."],"expected_primary_and_slice_effects":"Provisional prediction: seed-42 unweighted four-category HR@10 exceeds the observed incumbent mean of 0.56325 by more than 0.005 and exceeds the generated control. Report all four category effects and available history-length slices, including regressions; no slice-specific benefit is established.","falsification_condition":"Reject implementation admission if initialization equivalence, the conditioning diagnostic, causality or scoring contracts fail. Do not advance if seed-42 candidate-minus-incumbent mean HR@10 is <=0.005, candidate-minus-control is <=0, or the frozen eligibility gate fails. If eligible, apply only the existing confirmation rules to independent seeds 202609291 and 202609292. A control advantage or failure to reproduce the effect weakens the input-conditioning explanation.","gap_ids":["amazon-next-v7-round-5-residual-conditioning"],"guardrails":["Paths are relative to model/: model.py and complete control-1.py. Preserve unrelated code, imports, configuration, helpers and method signatures.","Preserve 200 epochs, 200 batches, evaluation every 5 epochs, patience 20 and public-validation-only checkpoint selection.","Preserve stable pairwise BPR, evaluation seed 20260923, 1000 users, positive plus 99 unique negatives and unweighted four-category HR@10 aggregation.","The reservation covers up to 12 candidate fits, 12 generated-control fits, missing incumbent comparator fits and overhead; verify cost before execution without shortening the protocol.","No training or source changes are part of this research response."],"insertion_contract":"{\"schema\":\"nextitnet-method-scope-v1\",\"allowed_methods\":[\"NextItNetBlock.__init__\",\"NextItNetBlock.forward\"],\"rationale\":\"Add matched zero-initialized per-channel gate parameters in each block. Candidate scales the existing causal update using the incoming state; the complete generated control scales it using the update. Preserve every other method and the frozen protocol.\"}","mechanism":"Compare one input-conditioned residual gate against selected_v3 and a parameter-matched update-conditioned gate. The matched gate control separates the proposed conditioning choice from the shared addition of gate parameters, subject to remaining optimization differences.","method_ids":["amazon-next-v7-input-conditioned-residual"],"origin":"agent_hypothesis","proposal_id":"amazon-next-v7-round-5","protocol_hash":"54fbd25c87110ea1b813f57c205b1725ceb0fb77b1e61ed9a331e3fe90dc6d31","seeds":[42,202609291,202609292],"target_component_ids":["model.py: NextItNetBlock.__init__","model.py: NextItNetBlock.forward"],"task_id":"amazon-research-9b51668f86f6f404","train_protocol_hash":"54fbd25c87110ea1b813f57c205b1725ceb0fb77b1e61ed9a331e3fe90dc6d31","tuning_allowance":"None. Fix the gate formula, zero initialization and matched control before evaluation; make no category-specific or confirmation-driven adjustments.","visibility":"public"},"id":"amazon-research-9b51668f86f6f404-f83a2bcad14a55d9-proposal","type":"Proposal"},{"attrs":{"candidate":0.63,"counterevidence":false,"dataset":"Movies_and_TV","effects":{"amazon-next-v7-round-5-control-1":0.020000000000000018,"selected_v3":0.01100000000000001},"evidence_dependency_ids":["amazon-research-9b51668f86f6f404-f83a2bcad14a55d9-development"],"independent_unit":false,"origin":"local_evidence","partition":"development","protocol_hash":"54fbd25c87110ea1b813f57c205b1725ceb0fb77b1e61ed9a331e3fe90dc6d31","report_ref":{"availability":"available","sha256":"78d32fcc624b508fe3c1c8793efc68dd22309682afa65e9419c6f04a4f8ce225","size":10888},"seed":42,"task_id":"amazon-research-9b51668f86f6f404","visibility":"public"},"id":"amazon-research-9b51668f86f6f404-f83a2bcad14a55d9-slice-04f380acbf2b","type":"Observation"},{"attrs":{"candidate":0.543,"counterevidence":true,"dataset":"Industrial_and_Scientific","effects":{"amazo