esults for other mechanisms are separate history, not relations in the supplied graph; they do not establish this mechanism."],"cheapest_discriminating_test":"On CPU, hold a block''s weights fixed and feed two causal inputs with different current states. Verify that the proposed residual gate changes by input, while the matched control''s gate is constant across inputs. Check that both produce the same 0.5 gate at initialization. This tests the architectural distinction; ranking benefit requires frozen-protocol fits.","gap_id":"amazon-next-v7-round-10","model_version":"selected_v3","observation_refs":["current-baseline-0b9b74a7cf77fd8200690b25"],"origin":"agent_hypothesis","predicted_observations":["The candidate''s residual update multiplier varies with the current causal state; the control''s multiplier is input-independent.","If conditional suppression helps ranking, the candidate exceeds selected_v3 by more than 0.005 in four-category mean HR@10 and exceeds the generated control by more than zero.","Electronics may show the largest category gain, but category effects and confirmation results remain unknown."],"protocol_hash":"54fbd25c87110ea1b813f57c205b1725ceb0fb77b1e61ed9a331e3fe90dc6d31","status":"unknown","suspected_capability":"Provisional hypothesis: condition each convolutional residual update on the current causal state so the encoder can reduce an unhelpful update.","task_context":"Observed in the sole supplied graph node: seed-42 HR@10 is 0.619, 0.546, 0.445 and 0.643 for Movies_and_TV, Industrial_and_Scientific, Electronics and CDs_and_Vinyl. The graph has no edges, counterevidence nodes or revision entries. These aggregates do not identify a causal defect. Earlier experiment readouts and counterevidence appear in history outside this graph and provide no confirmation of the proposed gate.","task_id":"amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce","visibility":"public"},"id":"amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce-ded3cc3280da1a1b-gap","type":"GapHypothesis"},{"attrs":{"baseline":"selected_v3","candidate":"amazon-next-v7-round-10-model","candidate_minus_baseline":-0.004249999999999976,"candidate_minus_control":-0.00824999999999998,"control":"amazon-next-v7-round-10-control-1","control_minus_baseline":0.0040000000000000036,"design":{"alternative_explanations":["A gain could come from the changed residual scale or added parameters rather than input-dependent gating.","The control''s static gate may optimize differently despite matching parameter count and initialization.","Category sampling, stochastic optimization and public-validation checkpoint choice may explain small gains."],"falsification_condition":"The ranking hypothesis fails its development gate if mean HR@10 improvement over selected_v3 is at most 0.005 or improvement over the generated control is at most zero. The proposed mechanism is unsupported if the CPU input-variation test does not distinguish the gates. Passing development would still require the bound confirmation seeds.","insertion_contract":"{\"schema\":\"nextitnet-method-scope-v1\",\"allowed_methods\":[\"NextItNetBlock.__init__\",\"NextItNetBlock.forward\"],\"rationale\":\"Candidate and generated control add identical per-block linear gate parameters and apply their gates to the second convolution residual update. Only the candidate feeds the current causal state to the gate; the control feeds ones. No other methods need changes.\"}","mechanism":"Compare a current-state-dependent residual gate with both the incumbent ungated blocks and a parameter-matched input-independent gate. The contrast tests whether conditional suppression adds value beyond gate capacity and initial residual scaling.","predicted_observations":["The candidate''s residual update multiplier varies with the current causal state; the control''s multiplier is input-independent.","If conditional suppression helps ranking, the candidate exceeds selected_v3 by more than 0.005 in four-category mean HR@10 and exceeds the generated control by more than zero.","Electronics may show the largest category gain, but category effects and confirmation results remain unknown."]},"design_hash":"f30190a50977000f49bef23d2cde2c3545f71e7b5c040c8d5bd3d7c16e1cf6e0","evidence_dependency_ids":["amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce-ded3cc3280da1a1b-development"],"independent_unit":false,"kind":"mechanism_comparison","mechanism_status":"unknown","next_step":"Assess whether the implemented contrast isolates the proposed mechanism; design a discriminating follow-up for competing explanations.","origin":"local_evidence","partition":"development","protocol_hash":"54fbd25c87110ea1b813f57c205b1725ceb0fb77b1e61ed9a331e3fe90dc6d31","qualification":"Paired development observation, not causal proof or independent replication.","report_ref":{"availability":"available","sha256":"0f33c8a978375761bc1d1855d7def25d69310e072020fae2ae6d0a67ea3ba100","size":10837},"slices":[{"candidate_minus_control":-0.02100000000000002,"dataset":"Movies_and_TV","seed":42},{"candidate_minus_control":-0.008000000000000007,"dataset":"Industrial_and_Scientific","seed":42},{"candidate_minus_control":0.0050000000000000044,"dataset":"Electronics","seed":42},{"candidate_minus_control":-0.009000000000000008,"dataset":"CDs_and_Vinyl","seed":42}],"source_hashes":{"amazon-next-v7-round-10-control-1":"392e726e924eba19cb3d0418c4b4989c59585042e6d9c663c4fb1925d0217145","amazon-next-v7-round-10-model":"5a4005b1e010b82cd45cf486b9a11f2e462beede32aba80e1d99110d7aab6b54","selected_v3":"ae556df7a0c0808bd7c2dc5dc912eb5546a0abe297cc73683a395bddb8240635"},"task_id":"amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce","visibility":"public"},"id":"amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce-ded3cc3280da1a1b-mechanism-fcded12be704cbe2","type":"Observation"},{"attrs":{"cost":"Plan up to 800000 of the 1121676 remaining GPU-budget units for 24 candidate/control category-seed fits, up to eight missing incumbent confirmation fits, and overhead. No protocol shortening.","insertion_points":["model.py: NextItNetBlock.__init__","model.py: NextItNetBlock.forward"],"mechanism":"Agent hypothesis. In each block, multiply the second convolution''s post-activation residual output by sigmoid(W LayerNorm(x) + b), then add the original residual. Initialize W and b to zero, giving a 0.5 multiplier initially. The generated control uses the same per-block linear gate and initialization but feeds it an all-ones tensor, producing an input-independent learned channel multiplier. This isolates state dependence from adding a gate and changing initial residual scale.","method_id":"causal_state_residual_gate_v1","origin":"agent_hypothesis","prerequisites":["Independent initialization for each category and seed.","Apply the identical frozen training, checkpoint-selection and ranking protocol to candidate and controls.","Keep all gate inputs causal and preserve the existing per-block padding mask in encode_sequence."],"protocol_hash":"54fbd25c87110ea1b813f57c205b1725ceb0fb77b1e61ed9a331e3fe90dc6d31","sources":[],"task_id":"amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce","tensor_constraints":["Block input and output remain [batch, length, hidden_units].","Each gate has shape [batch, length, hidden_units] and depends only on the state at its own position.","encode_sequence remains causal and returns masked [batch, length, hidden_units] representations.","forward and score_candidates consume those same final representations; candidate scores remain item_emb(candidates) @ encode_sequence(seq)[0,-1]."],"visibility":"public"},"id":"amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce-ded3cc3280da1a1b-method","type":"Method"},{"attrs":{"action":"add","alternative_explanations":["A gain could come from the changed residual scale or added parameters rather than input-dependent gating.","The control''s static gate may optimize differently despite matching parameter count and initialization.","Category sampling, stochastic optimization and public-validation checkpoint choice may explain small gains."],"base_model_id":"selected_v3","budget":800000,"controls":["selected_v3","amazon-next-v7-round-10-control-1"],"correctness_checks":["CPU fixed-weight test: candidate gate changes with current state; control gate remains constant; both equal 0.5 at initialization.","After a parameter update, verify causal input gradients, zero padding gradients, finite empty-history output and batch independence.","Verify forward uses encode_sequence output and score_candidates equals the required tail-state dot product after learning.","Verify candidate and control have matching gate parameter shapes and independent fresh initialization."],"expected_primary_and_slice_effects":"Hypothesis: four-category mean HR@10 improves by more than 0.005 over selected_v3 and by more than zero over the static-gate control. Electronics, whose observed baseline HR@10 is 0.445, is the prespecified slice expected to benefit most. Report all four category effects, including negative ones.","falsification_condition":"The ranking hypothesis fails its development gate if mean HR@10 improvement over selected_v3 is at most 0.005 or improvement over the generated control is at most zero. The proposed mechanism is unsupported if the CPU input-variation test does not distinguish the gates. Passing development would still require the bound confirmation seeds.","gap_ids":["amazon-next-v7-round-10"],"guardrails":["Do not change the frozen protocol, imports, module configuration, training/data helpers or method signatures.","Limit any subsequent source changes to the declared methods in model.py and a complete control-1.py module.","Do not infer a mechanism conclusion from development selection or from the single graph observation."],"insertion_contract":"{\"schema\":\"nextitnet-method-scope-v1\",\"allowed_methods\":[\"NextItNetBlock.__init__\",\"NextItNetBlock.forward\"],\"rationale\":\"Candidate and generated control add identical per-block linear gate parameters and apply their gates to the second convolution residual update. Only the candidate feeds the current causal state to the gate; the control feeds ones. No other methods need changes.\"}","mechanism":"Compare a current-state-dependent residual gate with both the incumbent ungated blocks and a parameter-matched input-independent gate. The contrast tests whether conditional suppression adds value beyond gate capacity and initial residual scaling.","method_ids":["causal_state_residual_gate_v1"],"origin":"agent_hypothesis","proposal_id":"amazon-next-v7-round-10","protocol_hash":"54fbd25c87110ea1b813f57c205b1725ceb0fb77b1e61ed9a331e3fe90dc6d31","seeds":[42,202609291,202609292],"target_component_ids":["model.py: NextItNetBlock.__init__","model.py: NextItNetBlock.forward","control-1.py: NextItNetBlock.__init__","control-1.py: NextItNetBlock.forward"],"task_id":"amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce","train_protocol_hash":"54fbd25c87110ea1b813f57c205b1725ceb0fb77b1e61ed9a331e3fe90dc6d31","tuning_allowance":"No candidate-specific tuning; use the frozen hyperparameters and selection rule.","visibility":"public"},"id":"amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce-ded3cc3280da1a1b-proposal","type":"Proposal"},{"attrs":{"candidate":0.601,"counterevidence":true,"dataset":"Movies_and_TV","effects":{"amazon-next-v7-round-10-control-1":-0.02100000000000002,"selected_v3":-0.018000000000000016},"evidence_dependency_ids":["amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce-ded3cc3280da1a1b-development"],"independent_unit":false,"origin":"local_evidence","partition":"development","protocol_hash":"54fbd25c87110ea1b813f57c205b1725ceb0fb77b1e61ed9a331e3fe90dc6d31","report_ref":{"availability":"available","sha256":"0f33c8a978375761bc1d1855d7def25d69310e072020fae2ae6d0a67ea3ba100","size":10837},"seed":42,"task_id":"amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce","visibility":"public"},"id":"amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce-ded3cc3280da1a1b-slice-04f380acbf2b","type":"Observation"},{"attrs":{"candidate":0.535,"counterevidence":true,"dataset":"Industrial_and_Scientific","effects":{"amazon-next-v7-round-10-control-1":-0.008000000000000007,"selec