e selection threshold; not a mechanism refutation","effect":-0.004249999999999976,"effect_gate_passed":false,"evidence_dependency_ids":["amazon-next-v7-round-10-control-1-CDs_and_Vinyl-42","amazon-next-v7-round-10-control-1-Electronics-42","amazon-next-v7-round-10-control-1-Industrial_and_Scientific-42","amazon-next-v7-round-10-control-1-Movies_and_TV-42","amazon-next-v7-round-10-model-CDs_and_Vinyl-42","amazon-next-v7-round-10-model-Electronics-42","amazon-next-v7-round-10-model-Industrial_and_Scientific-42","amazon-next-v7-round-10-model-Movies_and_TV-42","selected_v3-CDs_and_Vinyl-42","selected_v3-Electronics-42","selected_v3-Industrial_and_Scientific-42","selected_v3-Movies_and_TV-42"],"independent_run_id":"amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce-ded3cc3280da1a1b-development-aggregate","kind":"derived_development_comparison","metric":"HR@10","minimum_effect":0,"origin":"local_evidence","partition":"development","protocol_hash":"54fbd25c87110ea1b813f57c205b1725ceb0fb77b1e61ed9a331e3fe90dc6d31","report_ref":{"availability":"available","sha256":"0f33c8a978375761bc1d1855d7def25d69310e072020fae2ae6d0a67ea3ba100","size":10837},"scientific_conclusion":"unknown","scientific_unit":"declared development seed aggregate; not additional independent runs or category slices","seed_ids":[42],"source_experiment_ids":["amazon-next-v7-round-10-control-1-CDs_and_Vinyl-42","amazon-next-v7-round-10-control-1-Electronics-42","amazon-next-v7-round-10-control-1-Industrial_and_Scientific-42","amazon-next-v7-round-10-control-1-Movies_and_TV-42","amazon-next-v7-round-10-model-CDs_and_Vinyl-42","amazon-next-v7-round-10-model-Electronics-42","amazon-next-v7-round-10-model-Industrial_and_Scientific-42","amazon-next-v7-round-10-model-Movies_and_TV-42","selected_v3-CDs_and_Vinyl-42","selected_v3-Electronics-42","selected_v3-Industrial_and_Scientific-42","selected_v3-Movies_and_TV-42"],"status":"success","task_id":"amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce","valid":true,"visibility":"public"},"id":"amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce-ded3cc3280da1a1b-development","type":"Experiment"},{"attrs":{"affected_components":["model.py: NextItNetBlock.forward","model.py: NextItNetModel.encode_sequence"],"alternative_explanations":["The lower Electronics HR@10 may reflect category difficulty rather than a limitation of the residual updates.","The existing convolutions may already learn when to suppress an update.","Initialization, optimization, checkpoint selection and repeated development selection may explain differences between trained variants.","Earlier development results for other mechanisms are separate history, not relations in the supplied graph; they do not establish this mechanism."],"cheapest_discriminating_test":"On CPU, hold a block''s weights fixed and feed two causal inputs with different current states. Verify that the proposed residual gate changes by input, while the matched control''s gate is constant across inputs. Check that both produce the same 0.5 gate at initialization. This tests the architectural distinction; ranking benefit requires frozen-protocol fits.","gap_id":"amazon-next-v7-round-10","model_version":"selected_v3","observation_refs":["current-baseline-0b9b74a7cf77fd8200690b25"],"origin":"agent_hypothesis","predicted_observations":["The candidate''s residual update multiplier varies with the current causal state; the control''s multiplier is input-independent.","If conditional suppression helps ranking, the candidate exceeds selected_v3 by more than 0.005 in four-category mean HR@10 and exceeds the generated control by more than zero.","Electronics may show the largest category gain, but category effects and confirmation results remain unknown."],"protocol_hash":"54fbd25c87110ea1b813f57c205b1725ceb0fb77b1e61ed9a331e3fe90dc6d31","status":"unknown","suspected_capability":"Provisional hypothesis: condition each convolutional residual update on the current causal state so the encoder can reduce an unhelpful update.","task_context":"Observed in the sole supplied graph node: seed-42 HR@10 is 0.619, 0.546, 0.445 and 0.643 for Movies_and_TV, Industrial_and_Scientific, Electronics and CDs_and_Vinyl. The graph has no edges, counterevidence nodes or revision entries. These aggregates do not identify a causal defect. Earlier experiment readouts and counterevidence appear in history outside this graph and provide no confirmation of the proposed gate.","task_id":"amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce","visibility":"public"},"id":"amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce-ded3cc3280da1a1b-gap","type":"GapHypothesis"},{"attrs":{"baseline":"selected_v3","candidate":"amazon-next-v7-round-10-model","candidate_minus_baseline":-0.004249999999999976,"candidate_minus_control":-0.00824999999999998,"control":"amazon-next-v7-round-10-control-1","control_minus_baseline":0.0040000000000000036,"design":{"alternative_explanations":["A gain could come from the changed residual scale or added parameters rather than input-dependent gating.","The control''s static gate may optimize differently despite matching parameter count and initialization.","Category sampling, stochastic optimization and public-validation checkpoint choice may explain small gains."],"falsification_condition":"The ranking hypothesis fails its development gate if mean HR@10 improvement over selected_v3 is at most 0.005 or improvement over the generated control is at most zero. The proposed mechanism is unsupported if the CPU input-variation test does not distinguish the gates. Passing development would still require the bound confirmation seeds.","insertion_contract":"{\"schema\":\"nextitnet-method-scope-v1\",\"allowed_methods\":[\"NextItNetBlock.__init__\",\"NextItNetBlock.forward\"],\"rationale\":\"Candidate and generated control add identical per-block linear gate parameters and apply their gates to the second convolution residual update. Only the candidate feeds the current causal state to the gate; the control feeds ones. No other methods need changes.\"}","mechanism":"Compare a current-state-dependent residual gate with both the incumbent ungated blocks and a parameter-matched input-independent gate. The contrast tests whether conditional suppression adds value beyond gate capacity and initial residual scaling.","predicted_observations":["The candidate''s residual update multiplier varies with the current causal state; the control''s multiplier is input-independent.","If conditional suppression helps ranking, the candidate exceeds selected_v3 by more than 0.005 in four-category mean HR@10 and exceeds the generated control by more than zero.","Electronics may show the largest category gain, but category effects and confirmation results remain unknown."]},"design_hash":"f30190a50977000f49bef23d2cde2c3545f71e7b5c040c8d5bd3d7c16e1cf6e0","evidence_dependency_ids":["amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce-ded3cc3280da1a1b-development"],"independent_unit":false,"kind":"mechanism_comparison","mechanism_status":"unknown","next_step":"Assess whether the implemented contrast isolates the proposed mechanism; design a discriminating follow-up for competing explanations.","origin":"local_evidence","partition":"development","protocol_hash":"54fbd25c87110ea1b813f57c205b1725ceb0fb77b1e61ed9a331e3fe90dc6d31","qualification":"Paired development observation, not causal proof or independent replication.","report_ref":{"availability":"available","sha256":"0f33c8a978375761bc1d1855d7def25d69310e072020fae2ae6d0a67ea3ba100","size":10837},"slices":[{"candidate_minus_control":-0.02100000000000002,"dataset":"Movies_and_TV","seed":42},{"candidate_minus_control":-0.008000000000000007,"dataset":"Industrial_and_Scientific","seed":42},{"candidate_minus_control":0.0050000000000000044,"dataset":"Electronics","seed":42},{"candidate_minus_control":-0.009000000000000008,"dataset":"CDs_and_Vinyl","seed":42}],"source_hashes":{"amazon-next-v7-round-10-control-1":"392e726e924eba19cb3d0418c4b4989c59585042e6d9c663c4fb1925d0217145","amazon-next-v7-round-10-model":"5a4005b1e010b82cd45cf486b9a11f2e462beede32aba80e1d99110d7aab6b54","selected_v3":"ae556df7a0c0808bd7c2dc5dc912eb5546a0abe297cc73683a395bddb8240635"},"task_id":"amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce","visibility":"public"},"id":"amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce-ded3cc3280da1a1b-mechanism-fcded12be704cbe2","type":"Observation"},{"attrs":{"cost":"Plan up to 800000 of the 1121676 remaining GPU-budget units for 24 candidate/control category-seed fits, up to eight missing incumbent confirmation fits, and overhead. No protocol shortening.","insertion_points":["model.py: NextItNetBlock.__init__","model.py: NextItNetBlock.forward"],"mechanism":"Agent hypothesis. In each block, multiply the second convolution''s post-activation residual output by sigmoid(W LayerNorm(x) + b), then add the original residual. Initialize W and b to zero, giving a 0.5 multiplier initially. The generated control uses the same per-block linear gate and initialization but feeds it an all-ones tensor, producing an input-independent learned channel multiplier. This isolates state dependence from adding a gate and changing initial residual scale.","method_id":"causal_state_residual_gate_v1","origin":"agent_hypothesis","prerequisites":["Independent initialization for each category and seed.","Apply the identical frozen training, checkpoint-selection and ranking protocol to candidate and controls.","Keep all gate inputs causal and preserve the existing per-block padding mask in encode_sequence."],"protocol_hash":"54fbd25c87110ea1b813f57c205b1725ceb0fb77b1e61ed9a331e3fe90dc6d31","sources":[],"task_id":"amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce","tensor_constraints":["Block input and output remain [batch, length, hidden_units].","Each gate has shape [batch, length, hidden_units] and depends only on the state at its own position.","encode_sequence remains causal and returns masked [batch, length, hidden_units] representations.","forward and score_candidates consume those same final representations; candidate scores remain item_emb(candidates) @ encode_sequence(seq)[0,-1]."],"visibility":"public"},"id":"amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce-ded3cc3280da1a1b-method","type":"Method"},{"attrs":{"action":"add","alternative_explanations":["A gain could come from the changed residual scale or added parameters rather than input-dependent gating.","The control''s static gate may optimize differently despite matching parameter count and initialization.","Category sampling, stochastic optimization and public-validation checkpoint choice may explain small gains."],"base_model_id":"selected_v3","budget":800000,"controls":["selected_v3","amazon-next-v7-round-10-control-1"],"correctness_checks":["CPU fixed-weight test: candidate gate changes with current state; control gate remains constant; both equal 0.5 at initialization.","After a parameter update, verify causal input gradients, zero padding gradients, finite empty-history output and batch independence.","Verify forward uses encode_sequence output and score_candidates equals the required tail-state dot product after learning.","Verify candidate and control have matching gate parameter shapes and independent fresh initialization."],"expected_primary_and_slice_effects":"Hypothesis: four-category mean HR@10 improves by more than 0.005 over selected_v3 and by more than zero over the static-gate control. Electronics, whose observed baseline HR@10 is 0.445, is the prespecified slice expected to benefit most. Report all four category effects, including negative ones.","falsification_condition":"The ranking hypothesis fails its development gate if mean HR@10 improvement over selected_v3 is at most 0.005 or improvement over the generated control is at most zero. The proposed mechanism is unsupported if the CPU input-variation test does not distinguish the gates. Passing development would still require the bound confirmation seeds.","gap_ids":["amazon-next-v7-round-10"],"guardrails":["Do not change the frozen protocol, imports, module configuration, training/data helpers or method signatures.","Limit any subsequent source changes to the declared methods in model.py and a complete control-1.py module.","Do not infer a mechanism conclusion from development selection or from the single graph observation."],"insertion_contract":"{\"schema\":\"nextitnet-method-scope-v1\",\"allowed_methods\":[\"NextItNetBlock.__init__\",\"NextItNetBlock.forward\"],\"rationale\":\"Candidate and generated control add identical per-block linear gate parameters and apply their gates to the second convolution residual update. Only the candidate feeds the current causal state to the gate; the control feeds ones. No other methods need changes.\"}","mechanism":"Compare a current-state-dependent residual gate with both the incumbent ungated blocks and a parameter-matched input-independent gate. The contrast tests whether conditional suppression adds value beyond gate capacity and initial residual scaling.","method_ids":["causal_state_residual_gate_v1"],"origin":"agent_hypothesis","proposal_id":"amazon-next-v7-round-10","protocol_hash":"54fbd25c87110ea1b813f57c205b1725ceb0fb77b1e61ed9a331e3fe90dc6d31","seeds":[42,202609291,202609292],"target_component_ids":["model.py: NextItNetBlock.__init__","model.py: NextItNetBlock.forward","control-1.py: NextItNetBlock.__init__","control-1.py: NextItNetBlock.forward"],"task_id":"amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce","train_protocol_hash":"54fbd25c87110ea1b813f57c205b1725ceb0fb77b1e61ed9a331e3fe90dc6d31","tuning_allowance":"No candidate-specific tuning; use the frozen hyperparameters and selection rule.","visibility":"public"},"id":"amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce-ded3cc3280da1a1b-proposal","type":"Proposal"},{"attrs":{"candidate":0.601,"counterevidence":true,"dataset":"Movies_and_TV","effects":{"amazon-next-v7-round-10-control-1":-0.02100000000000002,"selected_v3":-0.018000000000000016},"evidence_dependency_ids":["amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce-ded3cc3280da1a1b-development"],"independent_unit":false,"origin":"local_evidence","partition":"development","protocol_hash":"54fbd25c87110ea1b813f57c205b1725ceb0fb77b1e61ed9a331e3fe90dc6d31","report_ref":{"availability":"available","sha256":"0f33c8a978375761bc1d1855d7def25d69310e072020fae2ae6d0a67ea3ba100","size":10837},"seed":42,"task_id":"amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce","visibility":"public"},"id":"amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce-ded3cc3280da1a1b-slice-04f380acbf2b","type":"Observation"},{"attrs":{"candidate":0.535,"counterevidence":true,"dataset":"Industrial_and_Scientific","effects":{"amazon-next-v7-round-10-control-1":-0.008000000000000007,"selected_v3":-0.01100000000000001},"evidence_dependency_ids":["amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce-ded3cc3280da1a1b-development"],"independent_unit":false,"origin":"local_evidence","partition":"development","protocol_hash":"54fbd25c87110ea1b813f57c205b1725ceb0fb77b1e61ed9a331e3fe90dc6d31","report_ref":{"availability":"available","sha256":"0f33c8a978375761bc1d1855d7def25d69310e072020fae2ae6d0a67ea3ba100","size":10837},"seed":42,"task_id":"amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce","visibility":"public"},"id":"amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce-ded3cc3280da1a1b-slice-2d62719f6323","type":"Observation"},{"attrs":{"candidate":0.454,"counterevidence":false,"dataset":"Electronics","effects":{"amazon-next-v7-round-10-control-1":0.0050000000000000044,"selected_v3":0.009000000000000008},"evidence_dependency_ids":["amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce-ded3cc3280da1a1b-development"],"independent_unit":false,"origin":"local_evidence","partition":"development","protocol_hash":"54fbd25c87110ea1b813f57c205b1725ceb0fb77b1e61ed9a331e3fe90dc6d31","report_ref":{"availability":"available","sha256":"0f33c8a978375761bc1d1855d7def25d69310e072020fae2ae6d0a67ea3ba100","size":10837},"seed":42,"task_id":"amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce","visibility":"public"},"id":"amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce-ded3cc3280da1a1b-slice-7eca97b71893","type":"Observation"},{"attrs":{"candidate":0.646,"counterevidence":false,"dataset":"CDs_and_Vinyl","effects":{"amazon-next-v7-round-10-control-1":-0.009000000000000008,"selected_v3":0.0030000000000000027},"evidence_dependency_ids":["amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce-ded3cc3280da1a1b-development"],"independent_unit":false,"origin":"local_evidence","partition":"development","protocol_hash":"54fbd25c87110ea1b813f57c205b1725ceb0fb77b1e61ed9a331e3fe90dc6d31","report_ref":{"availability":"available","sha256":"0f33c8a978375761bc1d1855d7def25d69310e072020fae2ae6d0a67ea3ba100","size":10837},"seed":42,"task_id":"amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce","visibility":"public"},"id":"amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce-ded3cc3280da1a1b-slice-9a2a207b3cf3","type":"Observation"},{"attrs":{"category_contrasts_candidate_minus_control":{"CDs_and_Vinyl":-0.009,"Electronics":0.005,"Industrial_and_Scientific":-0.008,"Movies_and_TV":-0.021},"claim":"At development seed 42, four-category mean HR@10 was 0.559 for the state-dependent-gate candidate, 0.56725 for the static-gate control, and 0.56325 for selected_v3. Candidate minus baseline was -0.00425 and candidate minus control was -0.00825; control minus baseline was +0.004. The candidate failed its proposed >0.005 baseline and >0 control ranking gates. The control''s small positive baseline contrast qualified under the host''s baseline-positive confirmation rule, with no confirmation result supplied.","evidence_refs":["amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce-ded3cc3280da1a1b-development","amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce-ded3cc3280da1a1b-mechanism-fcded12be704cbe2"],"origin":"agent_hypothesis","partition":"development","protocol_hash":"54fbd25c87110ea1b813f57c205b1725ceb0fb77b1e61ed9a331e3fe90dc6d31","scientific_conclusion":"unknown","scope":"amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce","status":"provisional","task_id":"amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce","visibility":"public"},"id":"amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce-round-10-development-interpretation","type":"Claim"},{"attrs":{"evidence_refs":["amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce-ded3cc3280da1a1b-proposal","amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce-ded3cc3280da1a1b-mechanism-fcded12be704cbe2"],"gap":"A direct fixed-weight test of gate response to varying current causal state, together with replicated paired ranking contrasts, is absent from the supplied evidence.","next_discriminating_experiment":"At fixed weights, vary only the current causal state and measure the candidate and control gate outputs before and after learning; verify both start at 0.5 and only the candidate responds to state. Then fit the prespecified candidate, static-gate control, and baseline under the unchanged protocol on independent bound seeds, reporting every category and the four-category aggregate. This separates the architectural distinction from residual scale and tests whether any ranking advantage replicates. Do not treat the diagnostic or public development comparison as confirmation.","origin":"agent_hypothesis","partition":"development","protocol_hash":"54fbd25c87110ea1b813f57c205b1725ceb0fb77b1e61ed9a331e3fe90dc6d31","scientific_conclusion":"unknown","scope":"amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce","status":"provisional","task_id":"amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce","visibility":"public"},"id":"amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce-round-10-discriminating-test-gap","type":"MeasurementGap"},{"attrs":{"alternative_explanations":["Residual scaling or extra parameters may account for the static-gate control''s small baseline gain.","The static and state-dependent gates may optimize differently despite matched shape and initialization.","Sampling, stochastic optimization, and public-validation checkpoint choice may account for small category differences."],"claim":"The paired development contrast gives no aggregate ranking support for conditional residual suppression. The modest Electronics advantage over the static gate is a category-specific positive contrast, while three categories and the aggregate are negative. Matched parameter count and initialization, source admission, and synthetic execution checks do not prove that state dependence caused any category effect.","evidence_refs":["amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce-ded3cc3280da1a1b-mechanism-fcded12be704cbe2","amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce-ded3cc3280da1a1b-proposal"],"origin":"agent_hypothesis","partition":"development","protocol_hash":"54fbd25c87110ea1b813f57c205b1725ceb0fb77b1e61ed9a331e3fe90dc6d31","scientific_conclusion":"unknown","scope":"amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce","status":"provisional","task_id":"amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce","visibility":"public"},"id":"amazon-research-7f95d71c8c2149ce-round-10-mechanism-interpretation","type":"Claim"},{"attrs":{"counterevidence":false,"counterevidence_to":"candidate selection threshold; not a mechanism refutation","effect":0.0024999999999999467,"effect_gate_passed":true,"evidence_dependency_ids":["amazon-next-v7-round-5-control-1-CDs_and_Vinyl-42","amazon-next-v7-round-5-control-1-Electronics-42","amazon-next-v7-round-5-control-1-Industrial_and_Scientific-42","amazon-next-v7-round-5-control-1-Movies_and_TV-42","amazon-next-v7-round-5-model-CDs_and_Vinyl-42","amazon-next-v7-round-5-model-Electronics-42","amazon-next-v7-round-5-model-Industrial_and_Scientific-42","amazon-next-v7-round-5-model-Movies_and_TV-42","selected_v3-CDs_and_Vinyl-42","selected_v3-Electronics-42","selected_v3-Industrial_and_Scientific-42","selected_v3-Movies_and_TV-42"],"independent_run_id":"amazon-research-9b51668f86f6f404-f83a2bcad14a55d9-development-aggregate","kind":"derived_development_comparison","metric":"HR@10","minimum_effect":0,"origin":"local_evidence","partition":"development","protocol_hash":"54fbd25c87110ea1b813f57c205b1725ceb0fb77b1e61ed9a331e3fe90dc6d31","report_ref":{"availability":"available","sha256":"78d32fcc624b508fe3c1c8793efc68dd22309682afa65e9419c6f04a4f8ce225","size":10888},"scientific_conclusion":"unknown","scientific_unit":"declared development seed aggregate; not additional independent runs or category slices","seed_ids":[42],"source_experiment_ids":["amazon-next-v7-round-5-control-1-CDs_and_Vinyl-42","amazon-next-v7-round-5-control-1-Electronics-42","amazon-next-v7-round-5-control-1-Industrial_and_Scientific-42","amazon-next-v7-round-5-control-1-Movies_and_TV-42","amazon-next-v7-round-5-model-CDs_and_Vinyl-42","amazon-next-v7-round-5-model-Electronics-42","amazon-next-v7-round-5-model-Industrial_and_Scientific-42","amazon-next-v7-round-5-model-Movies_and_TV-42","selected_v3-CDs_and_Vinyl-42","selected_v3-Electronics-42","selected_v3-Industrial_and_Scientific-42","selected_v3-Movies_and_TV-42"],"status":"success","task_id":"amazon-research-9b51668f86f6f404","valid":true,"visibility":"public"},"id":"amazon-research-9b51668f86f6f404-f83a2bcad14a55d9-development","type":"Experiment"},{"attrs":{"affected_components":["model.py: NextItNetBlock.__init__","model.py: NextItNetBlock.forward"],"alternative_explanations":["The existing unconditional residual addition may be optimal under this protocol.","Any ranking change could arise from optimization, added parameters, or checkpoint selection rather than useful conditioning."],"cheapest_discriminating_test":"Without training, use identical fixed block inputs and convolution outputs in both arms. Verify that zero gate parameters reproduce the incumbent block exactly, then set nonzero parameters and vary the input while holding the convolution output fixed. The candidate gate should respond to the input; the matched control gate should not. This tests the implementation, not ranking benefit.","gap_id":"amazon-next-v7-round-5-residual-conditioning","model_version":"selected_v3","observation_refs":["current-baseline-0b9b74a7cf77fd8200690b25"],"origin":"agent_hypothesis","predicted_observations":["At initialization, both gated arms reproduce the incumbent residual output.","After nonzero gate updates, the two arms differ on fixed-state inputs designed to separate input conditioning from update conditioning.","If input-conditioned residual scaling helps ranking, the candidate exceeds both the incumbent and matched control under the frozen evaluation."],"protocol_hash":"54fbd25c87110ea1b813f57c205b1725ceb0fb77b1e61ed9a331e3fe90dc6d31","status":"unknown","suspected_capability":"Conditioning each causal convolutional update on its incoming state may improve ranking. The inspected block adds its update unconditionally; the supplied graph does not establish that this causes a deficit.","task_context":"Observed graph fact: selected_v3 seed-42 HR@10 is 0.619, 0.546, 0.445 and 0.643 across Movies_and_TV, Industrial_and_Scientific, Electronics and CDs_and_Vinyl, for an unweighted mean of 0.56325. The supplied graph has no counterevidence, alternative or revision edges; absence of those edges is not support for the proposed mechanism. The ranking explanation and predicted benefit are provisional. Historical development selection outcomes do not establish or refute this mechanism.","task_id":"amazon-research-9b51668f86f6f404","visibility":"public"},"id":"amazon-research-9b51668f86f6f404-f83a2bcad14a55d9-gap","type":"GapHypothesis"},{"attrs":{"baseline":"selected_v3","candidate":"amazon-next-v7-round-5-model","candidate_minus_baseline":0.0024999999999999467,"candidate_minus_control":0.0022499999999999742,"control":"amazon-next-v7-round-5-control-1","control_minus_baseline":0.00024999999999997247,"design":{"alternative_explanations":["Extra parameters or changed gradient flow, rather than input conditioning, may explain a gain.","Input and update gates can have different activation distributions despite matched capacity.","Stochastic training and public-validation checkpoint selection may explain small differences."],"falsification_condition":"Reject implementation admission if initialization equivalence, the conditioning diagnostic, causality or scoring contracts fail. Do not advance if seed-42 candidate-minus-incumbent mean HR@10 is <=0.005, candidate-minus-control is <=0, or the frozen eligibility gate fails. If eligible, apply only the existing confirmation rules to independent seeds 202609291 and 202609292. A control advantage or failure to reproduce the effect weakens the input-conditioning explanation.","insertion_contract":"{\"schema\":\"nextitnet-method-scope-v1\",\"allowed_methods\":[\"NextItNetBlock.__init__\",\"NextItNetBlock.forward\"],\"rationale\":\"Add matched zero-initialized per-channel gate parameters in each block. Candidate scales the existing causal update using the incoming state; the complete generated control scales it using the update. Preserve every other method and the frozen protocol.\"}","mechanism":"Compare one input-conditioned residual gate against selected_v3 and a parameter-matched update-conditioned gate. The matched gate control separates the proposed conditioning choice from the shared addition of gate parameters, subject to remaining optimization differences.","predicted_observations":["At initialization, both gated arms reproduce the incumbent residual output.","After nonzero gate updates, the two arms differ on fixed-state inputs designed to separate input conditioning from update conditioning.","If input-conditioned residual scaling helps ranking, the candidate exceeds both the incumbent and matched control under the frozen evaluation."]},"design_hash":"b3d8d45efe31dc34d42e105464858799446dff6732e07cd71a4c1f4330c1584a","evidence_dependency_ids":["amazon-research-9b51668f86f6f404-f83a2bcad14a55d9-development"],"independent_unit":false,"kind":"mechanism_comparison","mechanism_status":"unknown","next_step":"Assess whether the implemented contrast isolates the proposed mechanism; design a discriminating follow-up for competing explanations.","origin":"local_evidence","partition":"development","protocol_hash":"54fbd25c87110ea1b813f57c205b1725ceb0fb77b1e61ed9a331e3fe90dc6d31","qualification":"Paired development observation, not causal proof or independent replication.","report_ref":{"availability":"available","sha256":"78d32fcc624b508fe3c1c8793efc68dd22309682afa65e9419c6f04a4f8ce225","size":10888},"slices":[{"candidate_minus_control":0.020000000000000018,"dataset":"Movies_and_TV","seed":42},{"candidate_minus_control":-0.006000000000000005,"dataset":"Industrial_and_Scientific","seed":42},{"candidate_minus_control":-0.0050000000000000044,"dataset":"Electronics","seed":42},{"candidate_minus_control":0.0,"dataset":"CDs_and_Vinyl","seed":42}],"source_hashes":{"amazon-next-v7-round-5-control-1":"c0fb4d929d6e4bb1af5b9dc2366cdab8c7abe6f44a473257e312510d2e6ea019","amazon-next-v7-round-5-model":"c6ee9202203962ffd5237bf69042a89726f7f7a354621718af9df67281f9a30d","selected_v3":"ae556df7a0c0808bd7c2dc5dc912eb5546a0abe297cc73683a395bddb8240635"},"task_id":"amazon-research-9b51668f86f6f404","visibility":"public"},"id":"amazon-research-9b51668f86f6f404-f83a2bcad14a55d9-mechanism-c00d690da2c980bc","type":"Observation"},{"attrs":{"cost":"Two trainable hidden-width vectors per block; linear elementwise work per block position. Runtime and ranking effects are unmeasured.","insertion_points":["model.py: NextItNetBlock.__init__","model.py: NextItNetBlock.forward","control-1.py: the same two methods"],"mechanism":"Agent hypothesis. For block input x and existing convolutional update y, replace x+y with x+2*sigmoid(w*x+b)*y, using broadcast per-channel trainable vectors w and b initialized to zero. The generated control uses x+2*sigmoid(w*y+b)*y with identical parameter shapes and initialization. Both gates initially equal one; the contrast tests whether conditioning on the incoming state helps beyond conditioning on the update.","method_id":"amazon-next-v7-input-conditioned-residual","origin":"agent_hypothesis","prerequisites":["Admit complete candidate and control modules with changes confined to the declared methods.","Run CPU contracts before any fit.","Initialize each category, seed and arm independently under the frozen protocol."],"protocol_hash":"54fbd25c87110ea1b813f57c205b1725ceb0fb77b1e61ed9a331e3fe90dc6d31","sources":[],"task_id":"amazon-research-9b51668f86f6f404","tensor_constraints":["Keep each block input and output shape [batch,length,hidden], dtype and device.","Gate only the existing causal update; introduce no future-position reads.","Preserve encode_sequence output shape [batch,length,hidden], padding mask and finite empty-history behavior.","Preserve forward use of encode_sequence and score_candidates = item_emb(candidates) @ encode_sequence(seq)[0,-1], including after learning."],"visibility":"public"},"id":"amazon-research-9b51668f86f6f404-f83a2bcad14a55d9-method","type":"Method"},{"attrs":{"action":"replace","alternative_explanations":["Extra parameters or changed gradient flow, rather than input conditioning, may explain a gain.","Input and update gates can have different activation distributions despite matched capacity.","Stochastic training and public-validation checkpoint selection may explain small differences."],"base_model_id":"selected_v3","budget":1000000,"controls":["selected_v3","amazon-next-v7-round-5-control-1"],"correctness_checks":["With zero gate parameters and dropout disabled, both new arms match the incumbent block output within float32 tolerance.","With copied common weights and nonzero gate parameters, verify the fixed-state conditioning contrast and finite outputs.","Before and after synthetic parameter updates, verify prefix causality, zero padding-embedding gradient, finite empty histories, input immutability, batch independence and permutation equivariance.","Before and after updates, verify forward scoring identities, tail candidate scoring and save/load equivalence.","Verify candidate and generated control have matching parameter counts, state-dict structure and independent initialization."],"expected_primary_and_slice_effects":"Provisional prediction: seed-42 unweighted four-category HR@10 exceeds the observed incumbent mean of 0.56325 by more than 0.005 and exceeds the generated control. Report all four category effects and available history-length slices, including regressions; no slice-specific benefit is established.","falsification_condition":"Reject implementation admission if initialization equivalence, the conditioning diagnostic, causality or scoring contracts fail. Do not advance if seed-42 candidate-minus-incumbent mean HR@10 is <=0.005, candidate-minus-control is <=0, or the frozen eligibility gate fails. If eligible, apply only the existing confirmation rules to independent seeds 202609291 and 202609292. A control advantage or failure to reproduce the effect weakens the input-conditioning explanation.","gap_ids":["amazon-next-v7-round-5-residual-conditioning"],"guardrails":["Paths are relative to model/: model.py and complete control-1.py. Preserve unrelated code, imports, configuration, helpers and method signatures.","Preserve 200 epochs, 200 batches, evaluation every 5 epochs, patience 20 and public-validation-only checkpoint selection.","Preserve stable pairwise BPR, evaluation seed 20260923, 1000 users, positive plus 99 unique negatives and unweighted four-category HR@10 aggregation.","The reservation covers up to 12 candidate fits, 12 generated-control fits, missing incumbent comparator fits and overhead; verify cost before execution without shortening the protocol.","No training or source changes are part of this research response."],"insertion_contract":"{\"schema\":\"nextitnet-method-scope-v1\",\"allowed_methods\":[\"NextItNetBlock.__init__\",\"NextItNetBlock.forward\"],\"rationale\":\"Add matched zero-initialized per-channel gate parameters in each block. Candidate scales the existing causal update using the incoming state; the complete generated control scales it using the update. Preserve every other method and the frozen protocol.\"}","mechanism":"Compare one input-conditioned residual gate against selected_v3 and a parameter-matched update-conditioned gate. The matched gate control separates the proposed conditioning choice from the shared addition of gate parameters, subject to remaining optimization differences.","method_ids":["amazon-next-v7-input-conditioned-residual"],"origin":"agent_hypothesis","proposal_id":"amazon-next-v7-round-5","protocol_hash":"54fbd25c87110ea1b813f57c205b1725ceb0fb77b1e61ed9a331e3fe90dc6d31","seeds":[42,202609291,202609292],"target_component_ids":["model.py: NextItNetBlock.__init__","model.py: NextItNetBlock.forward"],"task_id":"amazon-research-9b51668f86f6f404","train_protocol_hash":"54fbd25c87110ea1b813f57c205b1725ceb0fb77b1e61ed9a331e3fe90dc6d31","tuning_allowance":"None. Fix the gate formula, zero initialization and matched control before evaluation; make no category-specific or confirmation-driven adjustments.","visibility":"public"},"id":"amazon-research-9b51668f86f6f404-f83a2bcad14a55d9-proposal","type":"Proposal"},{"attrs":{"candidate":0.63,"counterevidence":false,"dataset":"Movies_and_TV","effects":{"amazon-next-v7-round-5-control-1":0.020000000000000018,"selected_v3":0.01100000000000001},"evidence_dependency_ids":["amazon-research-9b51668f86f6f404-f83a2bcad14a55d9-development"],"independent_unit":false,"origin":"local_evidence","partition":"development","protocol_hash":"54fbd25c87110ea1b813f57c205b1725ceb0fb77b1e61ed9a331e3fe90dc6d31","report_ref":{"availability":"available","sha256":"78d32fcc624b508fe3c1c8793efc68dd22309682afa65e9419c6f04a4f8ce225","size":10888},"seed":42,"task_id":"amazon-research-9b51668f86f6f404","visibility":"public"},"id":"amazon-research-9b51668f86f6f404-f83a2bcad14a55d9-slice-04f380acbf2b","type":"Observation"},{"attrs":{"candidate":0.543,"counterevidence":true,"dataset":"Industrial_and_Scientific","effects":{"amazon-next-v7-round-5-control-1":-0.006000000000000005,"selected_v3":-0.0030000000000000027},"evidence_dependency_ids":["amazon-research-9b51668f86f6f404-f83a2bcad14a55d9-development"],"independent_unit":false,"origin":"local_evidence","partition":"development","protocol_hash":"54fbd25c87110ea1b813f57c205b1725ceb0fb77b1e61ed9a331e3fe90dc6d31","report_ref":{"availability":"available","sha256":"78d32fcc624b508fe3c1c8793efc68dd22309682afa65e9419c6f04a4f8