e small ranking contrast reproduces independently.","interpretation_rule":"A failed fixed-state contrast rejects the intended implementation distinction. A control advantage or failure to reproduce candidate gains weakens the input-conditioning explanation; reproducible gains alone remain provisional because optimization differences persist.","next_discriminating_experiment":"First compare both arms with copied common weights: verify zero-gate equivalence to the incumbent, then use nonzero gates and fixed convolution outputs while varying incoming states to test the conditioning contrast. If that diagnostic passes, evaluate the candidate, matched control, and baseline on the preregistered independent seeds 202609291 and 202609292 under the frozen protocol, reporting paired category effects including negative and null results.","origin":"agent_hypothesis","protocol_hash":"54fbd25c87110ea1b813f57c205b1725ceb0fb77b1e61ed9a331e3fe90dc6d31","scope":"amazon-research-9b51668f86f6f404","status":"provisional","task_id":"amazon-research-9b51668f86f6f404","visibility":"public"},"id":"amazon-research-9b51668f86f6f404-round-5-discriminating-test","type":"MeasurementGap"},{"attrs":{"alternative_explanations":["Added gate parameters or changed gradient flow may affect ranking.","Input- and update-conditioned gates may have different activation distributions and optimization trajectories.","Stochastic training and public-validation checkpoint selection may account for small differences."],"candidate_minus_control_by_category":{"CDs_and_Vinyl":0,"Electronics":-0.005,"Industrial_and_Scientific":-0.006,"Movies_and_TV":0.02},"claim":"At seed 42, the input-conditioned gate has a small positive four-category HR@10 contrast, but its proposed >0.005 incumbent improvement is unmet and the mechanism is unestablished.","effects":{"candidate_minus_baseline":0.0025,"candidate_minus_control":0.00225,"control_minus_baseline":0.00025},"evidence_refs":["amazon-research-9b51668f86f6f404-f83a2bcad14a